  sitemap.xml — Andrew Hoang (Hoang Tuan Anh)

  Every <loc> below byte-matches the <link rel="canonical"> on that page.
  A sitemap URL that disagrees with the page's own canonical is a conflicting
  signal and is one of the most common findings in a static-site audit.

  Deliberate omissions:
    - 404.html is not listed. It is noindex and must never appear in a sitemap.
    - _source/ is not listed. It is not published.
    - No <changefreq> and no <priority>. Google ignores both; including them
      only signals that a template was copied.
    - No <lastmod>. It is omitted rather than stamped with a date that was not
      verified. Add a real <lastmod> to an individual <url> only when that
      page's content actually changes — never bump all of them at once.

  The resume PDF is listed on purpose: it is an indexable, corroborating
  document that Google will index, and it backs up the dates and figures on
  the HTML pages.

  When a page is added or removed, update this file AND llms.txt together.
-->
